      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While these streaks of synchronicity feel incredibly uncanny, the mathematical probability of such events is surprisingly high when you consider the sheer volume of stimuli in your daily life. Since you are exposed to countless ads, songs, and signs, your brain is constantly registering minor matches. These coincidences are often best explained by confirmation bias—noticing and remembering the matches while forgetting the vast number of non-matches.",
